\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Finite-amplitude perturbation test. \textbf  {(a)} Vertical velocity at the shear-layer probe $(X/e,\,Y/e) = (1.3,\,1.2)$. The unforced run (grey, hidden beneath the dotted steady value) is followed at $t = \SI {10}{\milli \second }$ by the patch $v = \SI {2}{\meter \per \second }$ over $X/e = 0.1$--$2.1$, $Y/e = 0.8$--$1.6$. One damped cycle follows. \textbf  {(b)} Running r.m.s.\ relative deviation of all four monitors from their steady values (\SI {0.5}{\milli \second } window, logarithmic scale). The unforced run sits at $10^{-9}$--$10^{-10}$; after the patch the deviation rises by ten orders of magnitude and then decays, without any growing mode appearing.}}{15}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:uransp}{{8}{15}{Finite-amplitude perturbation test. \textbf {(a)} Vertical velocity at the shear-layer probe $(X/e,\,Y/e) = (1.3,\,1.2)$. The unforced run (grey, hidden beneath the dotted steady value) is followed at $t = \SI {10}{\milli \second }$ by the patch $v = \SI {2}{\meter \per \second }$ over $X/e = 0.1$--$2.1$, $Y/e = 0.8$--$1.6$. One damped cycle follows. \textbf {(b)} Running r.m.s.\ relative deviation of all four monitors from their steady values (\SI {0.5}{\milli \second } window, logarithmic scale). The unforced run sits at $10^{-9}$--$10^{-10}$; after the patch the deviation rises by ten orders of magnitude and then decays, without any growing mode appearing}{figure.caption.27}{}}
